# Phase 5 STOP-IN-CATALOG-WAIT: a turn in Ultra on openai/gpt-6-astra whose
# catalog could not be read at launch (the fake gateway's catalog answers 503
# for its first 3 s) waits, at its start, for the read its prompt started --
# which takes 10 s to answer -- and Ctrl-C lands 0.7 s into that wait. fx
# v0.0.16 ends the turn there, interrupted (`resolveForRequest`,
# `model_cache_runtime.zig:855-865@481104fd`; `orchestrator.zig:5893-5919`):
# the stop's one Cancelled line, idle, and no error -- not Ultra's refusal,
# which is a request's (`:7657`). The prompt waits out the failure's 5 s
# backoff, so it starts a read.
xfx: env XFX_SOUND=off
models models.json
modelsdown 3000
modelsdelay 10000
seed p5-stop-ultra-seed.json
nomodel
wait 8
snap before
type say something
key Enter
wait 0.7
key C-c
wait 1
snap stopped
wire stopped
until gone press ctrl+c again to exit
wait 1
snap settled
gwlog
